@tab Injected device loss, no audio, missing data, corrupt save, and unsupported feature cases
@tab Integration suite
@item Generated shaders
@tab Rebuild from pinned Rust GPU inputs and compare artifacts
@tab Shader change and release CI
@end multitable

Pixel comparison allows only a documented tolerance for backend floating-point
differences. It never hides missing geometry, wrong visibility, incorrect light
styles, or palette errors. Differential failures retain the smallest available
input, frame, trace, and environment report as CI artifacts without including
registered assets.

@node Performance budgets
@section Performance budgets

Budgets are measured after warm-up as median, 95th, and 99th percentile values,
with the spread reported. A result without build, driver, scene, and content hash
is not a release measurement.

The initial integrated reference profile is an Intel Core i7-8665U (4 cores / 8
threads), Intel UHD Graphics 620, 16 GiB RAM, NVMe storage, and current Bravais
at the test date. Before M2 acceptance, the maintainer records a second
high-performance discrete reference system for the 240 Hz target. Substituting a
machine requires a dated baseline note; it does not silently rewrite earlier
results.

@multitable @columnfractions .44 .58
@headitem Measure
@tab Target
@item Server frame, busiest campaign trace, integrated profile
@tab 99th percentile <= 2 ms
@item Client plus CPU render submission, GPU-driven scene
@tab 95th percentile <= 2 ms
@item Classic GPU mode, 1920 x 1080, integrated profile
@tab 99th-percentile frame time <= 16.7 ms in the reference scene
@item Enhanced GPU-driven mode, 2560 x 1440, discrete profile
@tab 95th-percentile frame time <= 4.2 ms (at least 238 measured frames per second, reported as the 240 Hz target)
@item Cold start to interactive no-data screen, warm page cache
@tab <= 2 s
@item Largest MVP map load after process start
@tab <= 500 ms on each reference profile
@item Peak process RSS during campaign reference run
@tab <= 512 MiB, excluding shared GPU accounting reported separately
@item Four-hour demo and map-transition soak
@tab No crash and no post-warm-up RSS growth above 5%
@end multitable

The reference scene is a committed input script run against a pinned free data
hash, plus a local registered-data replay. Timedemo reports present time, CPU
passes, and GPU passes separately. Vsync is disabled only for throughput tests;
latency tests use the shipping frame-pacing mode.

@node Acceptance
@section Acceptance

Tharsis v0.1 is accepted when all required M0--M5 items are verified; the free
campaign and local registered @file{id1} campaign can be completed; protocol 15
demo and save round-trips pass; the classic and enhanced presets pass their
visual suites; all declared performance ceilings are met or carry an explicit
release anomaly; and no S1 or S2 defect remains open.

Release artifacts build from a clean checkout on stable Rust, contain no game
assets, pass REUSE and dependency audits, include a generated SBOM, and install
from each required package definition. A release is not accepted solely because
a demo renders one attractive frame.

