@node Risks
@section Risks

@multitable @columnfractions .28 .16 .56
@headitem Risk
@tab Severity
@tab Control
@item Floating-point or ordering drift breaks demo and game fidelity
@tab High
@tab Manual transliteration for sensitive code, explicit promotions, no contraction, and first-field trace diffs.
@item Rust GPU nightly coupling blocks stable packaging
@tab High
@tab Shader-only cargo-gpu toolchain, committed artifacts, stable host builds, and a tested WGSL contingency.
@item Naga or driver output differs across backends
@tab High
@tab Shader validation, golden scenes, backend matrix, and artifact review on upgrades.
@item GPU-driven path is slower on integrated hardware
@tab Medium
@tab Benchmark Tier 1 against Tier 2 and select per adapter class; never assume indirect drawing is automatically better.
@item Experimental APIs destabilize the release
@tab Medium
@tab Keep mesh shaders and ray queries outside the MVP and disabled by default.
@item Malformed mods reach unsafe resource or command behaviour
@tab High
@tab Checked parsers, bounded VM, path confinement, command allowlist, and fuzzing.
@item Registered data cannot enter public CI
@tab Medium
@tab Synthetic and free-data CI, pinned licences and hashes, and a local registered-data release gate.
@item Scope expands into QuakeWorld or DarkPlaces
@tab High
@tab Preserve the non-goals and require a new PRD for either direction.
@end multitable

